<h1>Lego Set Tracker</h1>

<data-table columns="<%= columns %>" data="<%= data %>"></data-table>

<div class="introduction">
	<section class="description">
		<h3>What is this?</h3>
		<p>Lego Set Tracker is a simple application that helps you manage and track your Lego collection. Keep track of
			all the sets you own, view detailed information about each set, and see statistics about your collection.</p>
	</section>

	<section class="how-to-use">
		<h3>How to use</h3>
		<ul>
			<li><strong>Home:</strong> View this welcome page and overview of the app</li>
			<li><strong>Sets:</strong> Browse, add, and manage your Lego set collection</li>
			<li><strong>Total Pieces:</strong> View statistics and charts about your collection's piece count</li>
			<li><strong>Settings:</strong> Customize the application theme and preferences</li>
		</ul>
	</section>

	<section class="features">
		<h3>Features</h3>
		<ul>
			<li>Track all your Lego sets in one place</li>
			<li>View detailed information about each set</li>
			<li>Analyze your collection statistics</li>
			<li>Switch between light, dark, and system themes</li>
		</ul>
	</section>
</div>
